Model checkpoints

No model data is part of this package. The Laya decision checkpoints are
published at https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya (Apache-2.0) and
mirrored at https://models.curiosity.ai/laya/, from where this software
downloads them on first use; they remain subject to that licence.

Mica support (Laya.Mica) ports the request contract, prompt and readout of
Mica v0.5 4B by akivet (https://github.com/akivet/Mica, Apache-2.0); its output
codebook (src/Laya/Mica/codebook_255.json) and contract test fixtures
(tests/Laya.Tests/Fixtures/mica-contract-cases.json) are included unmodified.
The Mica weights are downloaded on first use from
https://huggingface.co/sky7350/Mica-v0.5-4B (Apache-2.0) or from
https://models.curiosity.ai/laya/mica/; Mica is a fine-tune of Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B,
Copyright Alibaba Cloud, Apache-2.0.

The checkpoints are trained on top of these base encoders:

  * answerdotai/ModernBERT-large — Apache-2.0
    https://huggingface.co/answerdotai/ModernBERT-large
  * jhu-clsp/mmBERT-base — MIT
    https://huggingface.co/jhu-clsp/mmBERT-base
